The IBBI is implementing the I&B Code, 2016 and by the aforesaid amendments to the Principal Regulations governing filing/settlement of claims against the debtor-company, has paved the way for filing of claims by creditors, other than financial and operational creditors. This has facilitated the filing of claims by a large number of home-buyers/flat-buyers, who had paid huge amounts of money to the Builders/Realtors for flats/homes being built by the Realtors, against whom now Insolvency Proceedings have been initiated and in respect of whom, the Interim Resolution Professional has invited claims. Once insolvency proceedings against the debtor-companies/realtors started and claims were invited by the IRP, the home-buyers were in a tight spot, as they were neither the financial creditors nor the operational creditors. To remedy this anomaly which was not envisaged/visualised when the I&B Code, 2016 and its Principal Regulations were drafted and being formulated, the IBBI quickly amended the relevant regulations, which has come as a big relief to such home buyers.

Home-Buyers Do Not Fall Under category of "Financial Creditors" or "Operational Creditors"

3. By prescribing and notifying the relevant Form-F for submission of claims by home-buyers, this has come as a big relief, especially for those creditors who are not financial creditors or an operational creditor. In this regard, it is pertinent to note that as per the provisions of the I&B Code, 2016, a "financial creditor" has been defined to mean a creditor to whom a financial debt is owed and the definition of the term "financial debt" includes money borrowed on interest. Similarly, an "operational creditor" means a person to whom a company owes operational debt, including those with respect to provision of goods or services.

Further, in terms of section 3(10) of the I&B Code, 2016, the term "creditor" means any person to whom a debt is owed and includes a financial creditor, an operational creditor, a secured creditor, an unsecured creditor and a decree-holder. In terms of section 3(11), "debt" means a liability or an obligation in respect of a claim which is due from any person and includes a financial debt and operational debt. In terms of 3(12), "default" means non-payment of debt when the whole or any part or instalment of the amount of debt has become due and payable and is not repaid by the debtor or the corporate debtor, as the case may be.

As per the terms of section 5(7) of the I&B Code, 2016, "financial creditor" means any person to whom a financial debt is owed and includes a person to whom such debt has been legally assigned or transferred to. Further, section 5(8) defines that "financial debt" means a debt along with interest, if any, which is disbursed against the consideration for the time value of money and includes –

(a)

money borrowed against the payment of interest;

(b)

any amount raised by acceptance under any acceptance credit facility or its de-materialised equivalent;

(c)

any amount raised pursuant to any note purchase facility or the issue of bonds, notes, debentures, loan stock or any similar instrument;

(d)

the amount of any liability in respect of any lease or hire purchase contract, which is deemed as a finance or capital lease under the Indian Accounting Standards or such other accounting standards as may be prescribed;

(e)

receivables sold or discounted other than any receivables sold on non-recourse basis;

(f)

any amount raised under any other transaction, including any forward sale or purchase agreement, having the commercial effect of a borrowing;

(g)

any derivative transaction entered into in connection with protection against or benefit from fluctuation in any rate or price and for calculating the value of any derivative transaction, only the market value of such transaction shall be taken into account;

(h)

any counter-indemnity obligation in respect of a guarantee, indemnity, bond, documentary letter of credit or any other instrument issued by a bank or financial institution;

(i)

the amount of any liability in respect of any of the guarantee or indemnity for any of the items referred to in sub-clauses (a) to (h) of this clause.

